  "text": "Recipe: Sweet Potato Sandwich\nCreator: Dr Sirisha Potluri\nCategory: Sandwich\nIngredients: sweet potato, spinach, arugula, avocado, tomato, cucumber, red onion, red cabbage, fresh chili, pickled jalapeños, chili, jalapeños\nCooking methods: bake, no-cook\nInstructions: Preheat oven to 400F/200C. Line a baking sheet with parchment paper. Cut the ends off sweet potatoes. Chop them into thick slices (see pic). Bake for 25 to 35 minutes or until brown. Remove from oven and let them cool. Wash all the vegetables. Slice & chop them. Stack them on sweet potato slices like a sandwich. The bottom and top layers will be sweet potato, with the middle section filled with all the other vegetables.\nNotes: A recipe with TUBERS (sweet potato), LEAFY GREENS (spinach, arugula, red cabbage), RAINBOW VEGGIES (tomato, cucumber, red onion), NUTS-SEEDS-AVOCADOS (avocado), HERBS & SPICES (chili, jalapeños). For the sweet potato, find a thick and long one to act as a replacement for bread (see pic).",
